    "Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__ConstructionLinework": {

        "meta": {
            "description"            : "Setting out linework standards for the Vale Lantern Designer: the datum levels, derivation triangles and member centrelines a fitter works to. Each entry carries BOTH the edge colour and the line type, because a construction line is only readable when the two agree - a red dash-dot is the ridge datum whether it is on screen in the web application, on a Layout sheet, or in a SketchUp model.",
            "version"                : "1.0.0",
            "lastUpdated"            : "11-Aug-2026",
            "consumedBy"             : [
                "Na__ValeTools__LanternImporter__Modules__ - creates the edge materials and the tags, then paints the imported setting out linework",
                "Vale Lantern Designer web application - VghLantern__Env3d__Config__SetOut.LineStyles is the upstream source these colours were transposed from"
            ],
            "sourceOfTruthNote"      : "Colours originate in the web application's 3D setting out view, which is where they were designed and where the on-screen legend reads them from. They are transposed here so SketchUp and Layout can use the same standard. If a colour is changed in one place it MUST be changed in the other; SourceStyleKey on every entry names the upstream key to change.",
            "keyGrammarNote"         : "SourceStyleKey is the web application's own entity key, formed as <Class>__<Family>. The importer looks entries up by that key, so neither side needs to know the other's naming.",
            "lineTypeNote"           : "Layout__LineStyleName values are taken from Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__Tags__.json -> LineStyleReference.AvailableLineStyles and are CASE SENSITIVE. 'Dash dot' is a legal name; 'Dash Dot' is not, and silently leaves the tag solid.",
            "edgePaintingNote"       : "Every entry sets EdgePainting__AdvancedSwapOff so Na__EdgeUtil__PaintDeepNestedEdges leaves this linework alone. Without it, Apply Line Thickness Tags finds an MTE colour with no entry in 03__LayoutDrawingLineworkTags__ and moves the edge to Untagged, stripping the setting out tags off an imported lantern. The tag names below must also appear in Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__Tags__.json -> ExportExclusions.AdvancedSwapOffTagNames for that protection to apply.",
            "GitHub__RepoUrl"        : "https://github.com/Adam-Noble-01/Plugins/tree/main/Na__Common__DataLib__CoreSuEntityStandards",
            "Data__URL"              : "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Adam-Noble-01/Plugins/main/Na__Common__DataLib__CoreSuEntityStandards/Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__EdgeMaterials__.json"
        },

